    "instructions": "How to Use the X-All Power Scrubber\n1. Charge the Scrubber\n\nBefore using the X-All Power Scrubber for the first time, make sure it is adequately charged. Disconnect the charger before using the device.\n\n2. Choose the Right Brush Head\n\nSelect the brush head that best matches the surface you want to clean. Use the appropriate head for corners, edges, or smooth surfaces.\n\n3. Attach the Brush Head\n\nSecurely attach the selected brush head to the scrubber before turning the device on. Make sure it is firmly in place.\n\n4. Prepare the Surface\n\nApply your preferred cleaning solution to the surface as needed. For best results, allow the cleaner to sit briefly on stubborn dirt or grime.\n\n5. Turn On the Scrubber\n\nPress the power button to start the scrubber. Hold the handle securely using the no-slip grip.\n\n6. Start Cleaning\n\nMove the scrubber slowly across the surface using light, controlled pressure. Let the rotating brush do most of the work rather than pressing down heavily.\n\n7. Clean Hard-to-Reach Areas\n\nUse the appropriate brush head to reach corners, edges, and other areas that are difficult to clean manually.\n\n8. Turn Off and Clean the Device\n\nWhen finished, turn off the scrubber. Remove the brush head and rinse or clean it according to the type of brush and cleaning solution used. Wipe the main unit clean and allow removable parts to dry before storing.\n\nImportant Usage Tips\nDo not immerse the entire device in water. The product is IPX5 waterproof, but waterproof does not mean submersible.\nAvoid using excessive pressure while scrubbing.\nChoose a brush head appropriate for the surface to help prevent scratching or damage.\nKeep the charging port and charging components dry before charging.\nTurn the device off before changing or removing brush heads.\nStore the scrubber in a clean, dry place when not in use.\n\nX-All Power Scrubber — Less Scrubbing, More Cleaning.",
